equest welcome"}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2018-10-20T04:25:45Z","updated_at":"2018-12-25T22:53:33Z","closed_at":"2018-12-25T22:53:32Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# Bug\r\n\r\nThanks for the great library, @samuelcolvin! I have been using it quite extensively in the past weeks and hope to contribute a possible bug (+ a suggested fix).\r\n\r\n* OS: **Mac OS**\r\n* Python version `import sys; print(sys.version)`: **3.6.4**\r\n* Pydantic version `import pydantic; print(pydantic.VERSION)`: **0.12.1**\r\n\r\nA self contained code snippet describing the bug:\r\n\r\n```py\r\nimport pydantic\r\n\r\nclass Foo:\r\n    pass\r\n\r\n# OK\r\nclass Bar(pydantic.BaseModel):\r\n    x: Foo\r\n    class Config(pydantic.BaseConfig):\r\n        arbitrary_types_allowed = True\r\n\r\n# throws RuntimeError: no validator found for <class '__main__.Foo'>\r\nBaz = pydantic.create_model('Bar', __base__=Bar, y=(Foo, ...))\r\n```\r\n\r\nI think that [this line](https://github.com/samuelcolvin/pydantic/blob/master/pydantic/main.py#L402) should be changed either to\r\n\r\n```python\r\nconfig = __config__ or __base__.Config\r\n```\r\n\r\nor to\r\n\r\n```python\r\nconfig = __config__ or __base__.Config or BaseConfig\r\n```\r\n\r\nif the meta-class does not set `__base__.Config = BaseConfig` by default. \r\n","closed_by":{"login":"samuelcolvin","id":4039449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMzk0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4039449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcolvin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcolvin/following{/other_